# Data-driven integration test for hackathon/house_move, run by tests/integration/test_house_move_hocons.py.
# Format: https://github.com/cognizant-ai-lab/neuro-san/blob/main/docs/test_case_hocon_reference.md
#
# Plan quality for C-20004 (Belfast to Leeds, completion 18 December 2026), whose old home has Northern Ireland's
# rules: domestic rates instead of council tax, and a driving licence that DVA cannot move to a GB address.
#
# Ground truth, from coded_tools/hackathon/house_move/data/obligations_rules.json with the facts the customer states
# in turn 2: the legal requirements are domestic rates with Land & Property Services for the old home, council tax
# at the new council (Leeds), contacting DVLA about the Northern Ireland driving licence, DVLA for the vehicle log
# book (V5C) and TV Licensing. There is no council tax for the old home.
#
# The test module issues a fresh session for C-20004 into HOUSE_MOVE_TEST_SESSION_C_20004.
{
    "agent": "hackathon/house_move",
    "timeout_in_seconds": 1200,
    "success_ratio": "1/1",
    "connections": ["direct"],
    "interactions": [
        {
            "text": "I'm moving house",
            "sly_data": {"session_token": ${HOUSE_MOVE_TEST_SESSION_C_20004}},
            "response": {
                "text": {
                    "keywords": ["Laganside"],
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "text": """Yes, those are all right. We both have Northern Ireland driving licences and one car, and our
son goes to Little Steps Creche. We have a TV licence. No post redirection, thanks. Please go ahead with the
plan.""",
            "response": {
                "text": {
                    "keywords": ["Leeds"],
                    "gist": [
                        """The reply gives a dated move plan in which each of these is marked as a legal requirement:
domestic rates with Land & Property Services (LPS) for the old home, council tax at the new council (Leeds), DVLA
for the Northern Ireland driving licence, DVLA for the vehicle log book (V5C), and TV Licensing.""",
                        """The reply does not say the customer must tell a council in Northern Ireland or Belfast
about council tax for the old home.""",
                        """The reply does not mark any of these as a legal requirement: energy, broadband, mobile,
home or car insurance, GP, nursery or creche, or the customer's bank.""",
                    ]
                }
            }
        },
    ]
}
